{
  "rules": [
    {
      "quote": "`model: inherit` を使う。`opus` などモデル名を agent 側に焼き込まない。世代が変わるたびに全 agent を追従更新する羽目になる。意図的に軽いモデルへ落とす場合だけ例外として明示 pin し、理由を書く",
      "rule": "In .claude/agents/*.md and .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md, use `model: inherit` and do not hardcode a model name like `opus`; only explicitly pin a model as an exception when intentionally using a lighter model, and document the reason."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`tools:` を列挙しない。省略して継承させる。MCP auth ツールまで並べた allowlist は harness 側の変更で腐る",
      "rule": "In agent or skill files, do not enumerate the `tools:` list; omit it to inherit tools from the harness, because explicit allowlists (including MCP auth tools) become stale when the harness changes."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`memory:` frontmatter は使わない。harness が `.claude/agent-memory/<name>/` (gitignore 済み) を注入してしまい、repo 追跡の `memory/agents/<name>/` 規約と二重になる。代わりに agent 本文で `memory/agents/<name>/MEMORY.md` を読む / 書くよう明示する",
      "rule": "Do not use the `memory:` frontmatter in agent files; instead, explicitly instruct in the agent body to read/write `memory/agents/<name>/MEMORY.md`, to avoid duplication with the harness-injected `.claude/agent-memory/<name>/` directory."
    },
    {
      "quote": "harness の memory prompt (`# Persistent Agent Memory` 以下) をコピペしない。以前は 5 agent × 約 150 行の stale なコピーが入っており、参照先も間違っていた",
      "rule": "Do not copy-paste the harness's memory prompt (the section under `# Persistent Agent Memory`) into agent files, as it leads to stale and incorrect references."
    },
    {
      "quote": "「自己チェック (報告前に実行)」チェックリストを書かない。`just run` のような **プロジェクトの品質ゲート** は書いてよいが、「報告前に再確認する」「ダブルチェックする」類の指示は削る",
      "rule": "Do not write self-check checklists (e.g., 're-verify before reporting' or 'double-check') in agent or skill files; project quality gates like `just run` are allowed, but remove any instructions to re-check or double-check before reporting."
    },
    {
      "quote": "例示を盛らない。`description` に `<example>` ブロックを 3 つ積むと探索空間を狭める。dispatch に必要な「何をする agent か / いつ使うか」だけ書く",
      "rule": "Do not include excessive examples in agent or skill files; avoid stacking `<example>` blocks in the `description`, and only state what the agent does and when to use it for dispatch."
    },
    {
      "quote": "詳細は skill へ progressive disclosure する。agent 本文に testing 方針や git 手順を再掲せず、`.claude/skills/` を参照する。CLAUDE.md も同様に「repo の簡潔な説明 + 非自明な gotcha + skill 索引」に絞る",
      "rule": "Use progressive disclosure by moving detailed instructions (e.g., testing policies, git procedures) into `.claude/skills/` and referencing them from agent files; keep CLAUDE.md limited to a concise repo description, non-obvious gotchas, and a skill index."
    },
    {
      "quote": "重複を作らない。同じ規約を CLAUDE.md と agent と skill の 3 箇所に書かない。1 箇所を正として残りはリンクする",
      "rule": "Do not duplicate conventions across CLAUDE.md, agent files, and skill files; write each convention in one canonical location and link to it from the others."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "rules": [
    {
      "quote": "`tests/e2e/` 配下の e2e シナリオは「実機 VRChat が必要だから人手検証」と扱わず、Claude セッション内で実行して動作確認・スクリーンショット確認まで行う。",
      "rule": "Do not treat e2e scenarios under `tests/e2e/` as requiring manual verification due to real VRChat; instead, execute them within the Claude session and perform action verification and screenshot verification yourself."
    },
    {
      "quote": "**実装タスクの完了条件として `just run` 通過だけでなく対応する e2e シナリオの実行 (`just e2e-test <NAME>`) まで Claude 側で回す**。",
      "rule": "For implementation tasks, consider the task complete only after both `just run` passes and the corresponding e2e scenario is executed via `just e2e-test <NAME>` by Claude."
    },
    {
      "quote": "機能を実装したら **対応する e2e シナリオを書く / 既存シナリオを更新する** ことを既定にする。明示的に不要と判断できる場合 (純粋ロジックのみで実機影響なし、共有ヘルパの軽微な改修など) のみスキップしてよい",
      "rule": "When implementing a feature, by default write a corresponding e2e scenario or update an existing one; you may skip only when you can explicitly determine it is unnecessary (e.g., pure logic with no real-device impact, minor changes to shared helpers)."
    },
    {
      "quote": "実装ステップで e2e シナリオを書いたら、続けて `just e2e-test <NAME>` を実行する",
      "rule": "After writing an e2e scenario in an implementation step, immediately run `just e2e-test <NAME>`."
    },
    {
      "quote": "SSH 越しでも `just e2e-test <NAME>` だけで OK。justfile が `DISPLAY=\"${DISPLAY:-:0}\" XAUTHORITY=\"${XAUTHORITY:-$HOME/.Xauthority}\" uv run python ...` の形でデフォルトフォールバックを持っているため、env を自分で前置する必要はない",
      "rule": "Even over SSH, running `just e2e-test <NAME>` alone is sufficient; do not prefix environment variables yourself because the justfile provides default fallbacks for DISPLAY and XAUTHORITY."
    },
    {
      "quote": "出力 `_e2e_artifacts/<scenario>/<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS>/<label>.png` を `Read` ツールで開いて期待通りか検証する",
      "rule": "Open the output screenshot at `_e2e_artifacts/<scenario>/<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS>/<label>.png` using the Read tool and verify it matches expectations."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`PASS:` で終わっていてもスクリーンショット内容に異常があれば failure 扱いで再修正する",
      "rule": "Even if the e2e test ends with `PASS:`, treat it as a failure and fix it again if the screenshot content shows any abnormality."
    },
    {
      "quote": "実機都合 (Steam 起動忘れ、Wayland native セッション、uinput 権限不足など) で失敗したらユーザーに環境を依頼するが、それは「人手検証」ではなく「環境セットアップ依頼」として明確に区別する",
      "rule": "If the e2e test fails due to real-device conditions (e.g., Steam not started, Wayland native session, insufficient uinput permissions), request the environment from the user, but clearly distinguish this as an 'environment setup request' rather than 'manual verification'."
    },
    {
      "quote": "エージェントを起動するときも「e2e シナリオの実行は本タスクの責任外」と書かない。実装エージェントには「書いて `just run` を pass させる」までを依頼し、`just e2e-test` は親 (Claude 本体) が実行する分担にする",
      "rule": "When launching an agent, do not write that executing e2e scenarios is outside the task's responsibility; instead, delegate to the implementation agent only up to writing the scenario and passing `just run`, while the parent (Claude itself) runs `just e2e-test`."
    },
    {
      "quote": "完了報告のテンプレ: 「`just run` 緑 + `just e2e-test <NAME>` 緑 + スクショ確認 OK」までを 1 セットにする",
      "rule": "Use the completion report template: report as one set that `just run` is green, `just e2e-test <NAME>` is green, and screenshot verification is OK."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "rules": [
    {
      "quote": "`vrcpilot.launch()` の 0.3.0 デフォルト経路は Linux では `umu-run /path/to/VRChat/launch.exe`。**`GAMEID` env を渡してはいけない**。",
      "rule": "When launching VRChat via vrcpilot.launch() on Linux using the direct-spawn path (umu-run launch.exe), do not pass the GAMEID environment variable."
    },
    {
      "quote": "Linux で direct-spawn を試すとき、もし WINEPREFIX を明示せず umu-launcher の素の prefix で起動する設計を続けるなら、**GAMEID は引き続き付けない**。今後 `--app-id` 系の引数を追加するときも direct-spawn では env に乗せない",
      "rule": "When using Linux direct-spawn with umu-launcher's default prefix (no explicit WINEPREFIX), continue to omit GAMEID; also, when adding future --app-id style arguments, do not put them into the environment for direct-spawn."
    },
    {
      "quote": "ProtonFixes upstream に VRChat (438100) の正規 fix エントリが追加されたら、GAMEID 付与を復活させる価値があるかもしれない。ただし最初に「GAMEID=438100 を渡しても DLL エラーで死なないこと」を実機で再確認すること",
      "rule": "If ProtonFixes upstream adds a proper fix entry for VRChat (app id 438100), you may consider restoring GAMEID, but first verify on real hardware that passing GAMEID=438100 does not cause a DLL error crash."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`tests/vrcpilot/process/test_launch.py::TestLaunchDirectSpawnLinux::test_does_not_set_gameid_env` がこの仕様をロックインしている。将来「GAMEID をなぜ付けてないんだっけ?」となった人はこのテストとコメントを読む",
      "rule": "When wondering why GAMEID is not set in Linux direct-spawn, read the test `tests/vrcpilot/process/test_launch.py::TestLaunchDirectSpawnLinux::test_does_not_set_gameid_env` and its comments, as they lock in this behavior."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "rules": [
    {
      "quote": "Linux で `vrcpilot.launch(profile=0)` (direct-spawn) を呼ぶと、WINEPREFIX は `<library>/steamapps/compatdata/438100/pfx` を **自動マッピング**する。",
      "rule": "When calling vrcpilot.launch(profile=0) on Linux in direct-spawn mode, automatically map the WINEPREFIX to `<library>/steamapps/compatdata/438100/pfx`."
    },
    {
      "quote": "compatdata pfx が未初期化なら fail-fast で `VRChatSteamCompatdataNotFoundError` を送出する (silent fallback で別 prefix を作らない)。",
      "rule": "If the compatdata pfx is not initialized, fail fast by raising VRChatSteamCompatdataNotFoundError; do not silently fall back to creating a different prefix."
    },
    {
      "quote": "**`profile=0` は `launch()` / CLI の新デフォルト** (2026-05-25 変更)。無引数の `vrcpilot launch` / `vrcpilot.launch()` がそのまま「Steam アカウントで起動」になる。",
      "rule": "Make profile=0 the new default for launch() and the CLI (as of 2026-05-25), so that calling vrcpilot launch or vrcpilot.launch() with no arguments launches with the Steam account."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`via_steam=True` と `profile=0` は等価セマンティクスなので `validate_launch_args` も両者の同時指定を許容する (`profile>0` だけが `via_steam` と排他)。",
      "rule": "Treat via_steam=True and profile=0 as equivalent semantics, and allow specifying both simultaneously in validate_launch_args; only profile>0 is mutually exclusive with via_steam."
    },
    {
      "quote": "明示的に umu のデフォルト prefix を使いたい稀な場合は `profile=None` を渡す。",
      "rule": "Pass profile=None when explicitly wanting to use umu's default prefix in rare cases."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`--profile 0` は Steam-shared。`--profile 1, 2, ...` は per-profile isolated (vrcpilot-managed `$XDG_DATA_HOME/vrcpilot/profiles/<N>/wineprefix` を新規作成)。",
      "rule": "Treat --profile 0 as Steam-shared, and treat --profile 1, 2, ... as per-profile isolated, creating a new vrcpilot-managed wineprefix at `$XDG_DATA_HOME/vrcpilot/profiles/<N>/wineprefix`."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`--wineprefix=<path>` を明示すると `profile` 値より優先される (override の優先順位は `wineprefix` > `profile==0` > `profile>=1` > `profile==None`)。",
      "rule": "When --wineprefix=<path> is explicitly provided, it takes precedence over the profile value; the override priority order is wineprefix > profile==0 > profile>=1 > profile==None."
    },
    {
      "quote": "e2e 検証は VRChat 起動後の screenshot で判別: Home world が読み込まれていれば Steam アカウントが効いている (`--profile 0` 成功)、\"Welcome to the world of VRCHAT / Login with VRChat / Steam / Discord\" が出ていればログイン画面 = 独立 prefix。",
      "rule": "For e2e verification, use a screenshot after VRChat launches: if the Home world is loaded, the Steam account is active (--profile 0 succeeded); if the login screen with 'Welcome to the world of VRCHAT / Login with VRChat / Steam / Discord' appears, it indicates an independent prefix."
    },
    {
      "quote": "関連テスト: `tests/vrcpilot/process/test_linux.py::TestSteamCompatdataPfx` (path 構築)、`tests/vrcpilot/process/test_linux.py::TestResolveDirectSpawnWineprefix` (4 段階優先順位)。動作変更時は両方を更新",
      "rule": "When changing behavior, update both related tests: tests/vrcpilot/process/test_linux.py::TestSteamCompatdataPfx (path construction) and tests/vrcpilot/process/test_linux.py::TestResolveDirectSpawnWineprefix (4-level priority)."
    },
    {
      "quote": "pfx 未初期化エラーが出たユーザーへの案内は 2 つ: (1) `vrcpilot launch --via-steam` を 1 回走らせて pfx を bootstrap (2) `--wineprefix=<path>` で既存 prefix を渡す。fail-fast メッセージにこの案内が含まれている (`process/linux.py::resolve_direct_spawn_wineprefix`)",
      "rule": "When a pfx uninitialized error occurs, guide the user with two options: (1) run `vrcpilot launch --via-steam` once to bootstrap the pfx, or (2) pass an existing prefix via `--wineprefix=<path>`; include this guidance in the fail-fast message in process/linux.py::resolve_direct_spawn_wineprefix."
    }
  ]
}

{"rules": [
  {
    "quote": "vrcpilot のテストは以下の 4 区分で組み立てる。区分が決まればモック許容度・配置・スキップ方法が一意に決まる。",
    "rule": "Assemble vrcpilot tests using the 4 categories (unit, integration-with-fakes, integration-real, e2e); once the category is decided, mock allowance, placement, and skip method are uniquely determined."
  },
  {
    "quote": "**2026 年に方針が大きく改訂され、3rd-party ライブラリ表面のモックは禁止**になっている。",
    "rule": "As of the 2026 policy revision, mocking the surface of 3rd-party libraries is prohibited."
  },
  {
    "quote": "unit | `tests/vrcpilot/test_<file>.py` | 純粋ロジック | なし",
    "rule": "For unit tests: place them in `tests/vrcpilot/test_<file>.py`, target pure logic, and use no mocks."
  },
  {
    "quote": "integration-with-fakes | 同上、`tests/fakes/` から **自前 ABC** の fake を import | モジュール間結合 (ABC 越し) | **自前 ABC のみ** (`FakeCapture`, `FakeOCREngine`, `FakeMic` 等)",
    "rule": "For integration-with-fakes tests: place them in `tests/vrcpilot/test_<file>.py`, import fakes only from `tests/fakes/` that are self-owned ABC fakes, target inter-module integration across ABCs, and allow mocking only self-owned ABCs (e.g., FakeCapture, FakeOCREngine, FakeMic)."
  },
  {
    "quote": "integration-real | `test_<windows|linux>.py` / `window/test_*` / `capture/test_{windows,linux}.py` 等 | adapter / 3rd-party 結合点 (実環境) | 原則なし。実 daemon / Xvfb / loopback / 実 subprocess / 実 PNG",
    "rule": "For integration-real tests: place them in files like `test_<windows|linux>.py`, `window/test_*`, or `capture/test_{windows,linux}.py`, target adapter/3rd-party integration points in real environments, and use no mocks in principle; use real daemons, Xvfb, loopback, real subprocesses, and real PNGs."
  },
  {
    "quote": "e2e | `tests/e2e/` | 実 VRChat | なし",
    "rule": "For e2e tests: place them in `tests/e2e/`, target real VRChat, and use no mocks."
  },
  {
    "quote": "1. **実 resource** — `tmp_path`、実 subprocess の `sleep` / `echo`、loopback UDP、Xvfb、PipeWire null-sink、実 PNG fixture を実 OpenCV / RapidOCR に通す",
    "rule": "When verifying behavior, prefer real resources first: use `tmp_path`, real subprocess `sleep`/`echo`, loopback UDP, Xvfb, PipeWire null-sink, and real PNG fixtures passed through real OpenCV/RapidOCR."
  },
  {
    "quote": "2. **自前 ABC の fake** — `OCREngine`, `DetectEngine`, `Capture` / `CaptureLoop`, `Mic`, `Speaker` / `SpeakerLoop`, `OscSender` 等 vrcpilot が所有する抽象の差し替え",
    "rule": "When mocking is needed, prefer fakes of self-owned ABCs such as OCREngine, DetectEngine, Capture/CaptureLoop, Mic, Speaker/SpeakerLoop, and OscSender that vrcpilot owns."
  },
  {
    "quote": "3. **3rd-party ライブラリ表面のモックは禁止**: `pulsectl.Pulse`, `soundcard.*`, `subprocess.Popen`, `psutil.process_iter` / `psutil.Process`, `windows_capture.WindowsCapture`, `Xlib.display.Display`, `pyperclip.copy`, `proctap.*`, `inputtino.*`, `pydirectinput.*`, `time.sleep` 等",
    "rule": "Never mock the surface of 3rd-party libraries, including pulsectl.Pulse, soundcard.*, subprocess.Popen, psutil.process_iter/psutil.Process, windows_capture.WindowsCapture, Xlib.display.Display, pyperclip.copy, proctap.*, inputtino.*, pydirectinput.*, and time.sleep."
  },
  {
    "quote": "4. **自分のコードの内部関数モックも禁止**: `vrcpilot.controls.*.ensure_target`, `vrcpilot.process.pid.find_pids` 等を直接 `mocker.patch` で置き換えない",
    "rule": "Never mock your own code's internal functions, such as `vrcpilot.controls.*.ensure_target` or `vrcpilot.process.pid.find_pids`, by directly replacing them with `mocker.patch`."
  },
  {
    "quote": "プラットフォームやディスプレイに依存するテストは **import より前** に `pytest.skip(..., allow_module_level=True)` を置く。",
    "rule": "For tests that depend on platform or display, place `pytest.skip(..., allow_module_level=True)` at the top of the file before any imports."
  },
  {
    "quote": "関数単位の `@pytest.mark.skipif` だけだと、Linux runner で `import win32gui` のような import 自体が失敗して収集エラーになる。",
    "rule": "Do not rely only on function-level `@pytest.mark.skipif` for platform-dependent tests, because on a Linux runner the import itself (e.g., `import win32gui`) will fail and cause collection errors; use module-level skip before imports instead."
  },
  {
    "quote": "`sys.platform` の monkeypatch は禁止",
    "rule": "Never monkeypatch `sys.platform` in tests."
  },
  {
    "quote": "代わりに `tests/helpers.py` の `only_windows` / `only_linux` / `requires_x11_display` を使うか、ファイル分割 + module-level skip にする (旧方針では fail-fast `NotImplementedError` 検証のみ例外扱いだったが、新方針は一律禁止)。",
    "rule": "Instead of monkeypatching `sys.platform`, use `tests/helpers.py`'s `only_windows` / `only_linux` / `requires_x11_display` helpers, or split files and use module-level skip; the old exception for fail-fast `NotImplementedError` verification is now uniformly prohibited."
  },
  {
    "quote": "`tests/fakes/` には **自前 ABC の fake のみ**残す",
    "rule": "Keep only self-owned ABC fakes in `tests/fakes/`."
  },
  {
    "quote": "**新規追加禁止**: 3rd-party ライブラリ表面のミラー (`FakePulse*`, `FakeSoundCard*`, `FakeWindowsCapture`, `FakeXDisplay*`, `FakePopen`, `FakeProcess`, `FakePyDirectInput`, `FakeInputtino*`, `FakeMkv/Mp4/Wav` Muxer, `FakeProcessAudioCapture`, `FakePwRecordProcess` 等)",
    "rule": "Do not add new fakes that mirror 3rd-party library surfaces, such as FakePulse*, FakeSoundCard*, FakeWindowsCapture, FakeXDisplay*, FakePopen, FakeProcess, FakePyDirectInput, FakeInputtino*, FakeMkv/Mp4/Wav Muxer, FakeProcessAudioCapture, or FakePwRecordProcess."
  },
  {
    "quote": "既存の 3rd-party 表面 fake は整理対象 (別タスクで段階的に integration-real へ移行)",
    "rule": "Existing fakes of 3rd-party surfaces are candidates for cleanup; migrate them to integration-real tests gradually in a separate task."
  },
  {
    "quote": "共有 fake は `tests/fakes/{capture,ocr,...}.py` に集約し、テスト側は `from tests.fakes import FakeFoo` で明示 import",
    "rule": "Consolidate shared fakes into files like `tests/fakes/{capture,ocr,...}.py`, and have tests import them explicitly with `from tests.fakes import FakeFoo`."
  },
  {
    "quote": "fake の表面を広げる必要が出たらテストファイル内でサブクラス化せず正典クラス側に追加する",
    "rule": "If a fake's surface needs to be extended, do not subclass it in the test file; instead add the extension to the canonical class."
  },
  {
    "quote": "1. 純粋ロジック (環境依存ゼロ) → unit。モック不要",
    "rule": "When writing a new test: if it is pure logic with zero environment dependency, write it as a unit test with no mocks."
  },
  {
    "quote": "2. 外部協力者を差し替えないと書けない → integration-with-fakes。**自前 ABC** に限る。fake が無ければ `tests/fakes/` に追加する (3rd-party 表面 fake は追加しない)",
    "rule": "When writing a new test: if it cannot be written without replacing an external collaborator, write it as integration-with-fakes, limited to self-owned ABCs; if no fake exists, add it to `tests/fakes/` (but do not add 3rd-party surface fakes)."
  },
  {
    "quote": "3. 3rd-party の挙動依存ロジック → integration-real。Xvfb / PipeWire null-sink / loopback UDP / 実 subprocess / 実 PNG fixture。infra が未整備なら orchestrator に報告",
    "rule": "When writing a new test: if it depends on 3rd-party behavior, write it as integration-real using Xvfb, PipeWire null-sink, loopback UDP, real subprocess, and real PNG fixtures; if the infrastructure is not ready, report to the orchestrator."
  },
  {
    "quote": "4. 実 VRChat 必須 → `tests/e2e/<scenario>.py` として書き、`just e2e-test <name>` で実行",
    "rule": "When writing a new test: if real VRChat is required, write it as `tests/e2e/<scenario>.py` and run it with `just e2e-test <name>`."
  }
]}

{
  "rules": [
    {
      "quote": "`.claude/settings.json` の `permissions.allow` を毎セッション参照し、Bash・Read・Edit などのツール呼び出しはそのリストに収まる形に揃える。",
      "rule": "At the start of every session, read the `permissions.allow` list in `.claude/settings.json` and ensure all tool calls (Bash, Read, Edit, etc.) are within that list."
    },
    {
      "quote": "セッション開始時、または allow されているか怪しいコマンドを呼ぶ前に [.claude/settings.json](.claude/settings.json) の `allow` 配列を読む",
      "rule": "Read the `allow` array in `.claude/settings.json` at session start or before calling any command that might not be allowed."
    },
    {
      "quote": "`git -C <dir>` は `deny` なので使わない。cwd に居る前提でコマンドを書く。",
      "rule": "Do not use `git -C <dir>` because it is denied; write git commands assuming the current working directory is the project root."
    },
